speechtext:
I am sure of this, that there would be a great deal more satisfaction in the committee if the phraseology of the bill were examined by the counsel who has been mentioned. I am satisfied that the members of the committee are of the opinion that in obtaining the services of the counsel named we have one who has devoted himself so assiduously to the work that w'hen the bill is brought to the house it will be received without any of the acrimonious discussion which formerly obtained, and will be a measure acceptable to all parties.
Hon. CHARLES A. DUNNING (Minister of Finance): Mr. Speaker, I believe a reference to the terms of reference to the committee might clear up the matter. I would direct the attention of hon. members to the terms of reference as they appear in votes and proceedings of April 5. After indicating the names of the hon. members comprising the committee, the motion states that they be appointed to consider:
1.	A certain bill intituled: "An act respecting the franchise of electors and the election of members to the House .of Commons," and to make such amendments thereto as it deems advisable;
2.	A certain bill intituled: "An act respecting political expenditures," and to make such amendments thereto as it deems advisable;
3.	Such other proposed legislation relating to elections as may be referred to it by this house;
4.	The methods used to effect a redistribution of electoral districts in Canada and in other countries;
5. The evidence and report of the special committee appointed in the session of 1936 and reappointed in the session of 1937 to study the Dominion Elections Act, 1934, and the Franchise Act, 1934;
With power to call for persons, papers and records, to examine witnesses and to report from time to time.
It will be seen that there is a very much wider reference involved than merely a single bill. It seems to me the committee have a great deal of work to do of an intricate legal character, and if they unanimously desire to reengage counsel they have had in previous sessions, I do not believe, despite my desire to save .money, that I can enter any objection.

